// Dev-only (never shipped): load timeline, lag attribution, element timings and idle resource use for one route. Reports only; never edits the site.
//   node tools/diagnostics/perf-trace.mjs [--route optimized|optimized-taste|local|<any dir under the site root>] [--width 1365 --dpr 1 | --device "Pixel 7"] [--engine chromium|webkit]
//        [--cpu 4] [--net slow4g] [--seconds 10] [--scenario load|idle|scroll|sweep|pause|scrollback|interact|all] [--json out.json] [--baseline] [--hz 60]
//        [--css '<rules>']  inject CSS into every page (ablation experiments: measure what a rule costs; diagnostic only, not a fix)  [--trials human,fling,home,instant,anchor-about] [--from bottom|<scrollY px>]  (scrollback: where the page rests before scrolling back)
// all = load,idle,scroll,sweep. scrollback = scroll to the bottom, hold 4 s, scroll back up (human pace and fling) and attribute everything around the moment the hero tree scene re-enters. pause = prototype of phase-exact offscreen animation pausing (injected script only; not in all). --baseline also runs `local` (comparison only: the original is NOT a perf benchmark).
// Serves site/ (HW_SITE_ROOT overrides); writes report.json under HW_OUT or output/playwright/perf-trace/<run>/. Judge numbers against absolute budgets, not against --baseline.
// Chromium only for CDP parts (trace, layers, process CPU); --engine webkit reports in-page data (paint/LCP/long tasks/animation inventory) and skips the rest.
